tags: party_affairs

= Choosing our enemies

In our media and campaign materials, who should we consider as our main opponents?

[? if enemies != 0 : Previously, we had considered the [+ enemies +] as our prior enemies. Is a change of direction necessary? ?]

- @hp_enemy: The anti-establishment right is dangerous.
- @up_enemy: The Unitarists are the threat on the left.
- @vnpf_enemy: The regionalist populist will tear our country apart!
- @anti_kcp_enemy: All of the opposition parties are our enemies! We must do as Annastasia does , mercylessly and without end slander and attack our opposition!
- @easy_discard

@hp_enemy
on-arrival: enemies = "anti-democratic parties"; humanist_strength += 5; constitutionalist_strength += 5; rural_kcp -= 2; workers_hp -= 2; hp_relation -= 10

Attacking the anti-democratic right is the steadfast and safest choice. Little mistake to be done here. 

@up_enemy
on-arrival: enemies = "Unitarists"; neoforsvollrist_strength += 5; neoforsvollrist_dissent -= 5; workers_kcp -= 8; rural_kcp +=20;

The Unitarists are our enemies. They are the reason why the last regime failed!

@vnpf_enemy
on-arrival: enemies = "Peoples Front"; neoforsvollrist_strength += 5; nazi_urgency += 1; workers_vnpf -= 4;

[? if nazi_urgency == 0 or vnpf_r < 10 : The VNPF is a tiny party right now, with more bark than bite. Many in our party are questioning our choices. ?][? if nazi_urgency > 0 and vnpf_r >= 10 : The regionalist nationalists are the most urgent problem for us to deal with. ?]

@anti_kcp_enemy
on-arrival: enemies = "All anti-KCP parties"; neoforsvollrist_strength += 5; socialist_dissent += 8; humanist_dissent += 5; up_relation -= 15; hp_relation -= 5; vnpf_relation -= 5; workers_hp -= 4; workers_up -= 4; workers_vnpf -= 4;

Attacking all of our opposition at once is a dangerous strategy which will result in the radicalization of our political opponents. Tread lightly.

